   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Monday, November 9, 2015 at 2:37:01 PM UTC-5, Emmanuel Charpentier wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I have a model that compiles fine with rstan launched from my systemwide installation of R, but fails to compile when using the R interpreter in Sage.<br></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>It looks like a conflict between BH and the Boost that is included in Sage.<br><br><pre>/home/charpent/R/x86_64-pc-linux-gnu-library/3.2/BH/include/boost/lexical_cast/bad_lexical_cast.hpp:33:32: error: redefinition of ‘class boost::bad_lexical_cast’\r\n     class BOOST_SYMBOL_VISIBLE bad_lexical_cast :\r\n</pre><br><br>My guess is that Sage is configured to get its Boost headers before BH.<br><br>Ben<br><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
