   "date": "2015-11-10T06:09:44Z",
   "subject": "Re: My model compiles fine in (systemwine) rstan but not when using rstan from R in Sage (gcc problem ?)",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Tuesday, November 10, 2015 at 12:38:28 AM UTC-5, Emmanuel Charpentier wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hmmm... if the Boost headers are already included, it could be possible to test for them and condition the inclusion of BH headers to the absence of Boost headers, no ?<br></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>I&#39;m surprised that the header guards don&#39;t prevent the same file from being included twice. But I suspect part of the problem is that Boost in Sage still seems to be on 1.52, which is too old to use with Stan and probably has a lot of renamed files in the meantime.<br> </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">PS : How to formally report the problem (bug report) ?<br></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>We have GitHub repositories for reporting bugs, but I don&#39;t think this is a Stan bug. There have been reports from time to time of something like this happening on a Mac where an old Boost was installed to /usr/local/, but I think that was fixed for 2.8.<br><br>Ben<br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
}
